Choosing Capgemini means choosing a company where you will be empowered to shape your career in the way you'd like, where you'll be supported and inspired by a collaborative community of colleagues around the world, and where you'll be able to reimagine what's possible. Join us and help the world's leading organizations unlock the value of technology and build a more sustainable, more inclusive world.

Your Role

As a Senior DevSecOps Engineer, you will design and maintain secure CI/CD environments, build automated deployment pipelines, and support cloud and on‑prem infrastructure. You'll test and document solutions, advise project teams on DevOps automation, coordinate work in complex initiatives, and implement security practices to detect and prevent vulnerabilities throughout the development lifecycle.

Working with diverse and technically advanced solutions will allow you to build strong relationships with clients and continuously grow your expertise. You will be part of highly self‑organizing, independent teams that operate in agile and lean engineering environments, fostering continuous improvement and innovation.

Your Project

Application Development & Maintenance (ADM Center) provides comprehensive end-to-end IT services from business specification, through software development, implementation, to application maintenance using leading it technologies and management methods.

We enthusiastically institute solutions in the fields of DevOps, SRE, low-code, broadly understood Automation and AI.

We are hiring in Wrocław, Poznań and Gdańsk!

Your Tasks

* Design, build and support the continuous integration and continuous delivery environment putting general emphasis on security aspects for the needs of projects carried out in our department;
* Create deployment pipelines, scripts, administer virtual machines on cloud platforms and on prem;
* Test and document your solutions;
* Consult the needs of projects in the field of DevOps automation;
* Manage the work of teams implementing DevOps solutions in complex projects;
* Monitoring and identifying potential threads in the development cycle;
* Implementing tools and processes aimed at minimalizing the risk of releasing code with security vulnerabilities.

Your Profile

* Master's, engineer's, or bachelor's degree;
* At least 4 years of experience in working with CI / CD and / or cloud technologies;
* Knowledge of linux systems administration;
* Knowledge of any scripting language;
* Leadership and consulting experience;
* Good written and verbal communication skills (B2 English).

What You'll love about working here

